      "writtenOn": "2021-03-02T10:15:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmmm, to make sure you know what I mean, in motion_sense_switch_sensor_rate(), actually the body-detection is not affected, because the sensor-\u003edrv-\u003emanage_activity/list_activities is not handle the body-detection.\n\nThe body-detection is disabled by motion_sense_suspend():\n```\nstatic void motion_sense_suspend(void)\n{\n  ...\n  if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_BODY_DETECTION))\n    body_detect_set_enable(false);\n  ...\n}\n```\n(I also found that I forgot to re-enable the body-detection after resume. I will fix it later)\n\nHowever, adding the flag you mentioned might be a better solution. I will consider that if you still think my solution might be not working.",
      "parentUuid": "ef5ce9fa_da891797",
      "revId": "d406eff72656fd7c81b04f64cc6160597bdfe6f5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
